From a57bdb396b9e9740a2a621414fb27edfbd5e31c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Huang <sebastian_huang@accton.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:25:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] netifd: stop reading a wireless handler dump at end of file

handler_load() reads the dump of each wireless handler line by line
and only leaves the loop when f.error() reports an error. At end of
file f.read("line") returns null, but whether an error is reported
then depends on state left behind by earlier operations: with the
mac80211 handler it happens to be set, with others it is not, and
the loop spins forever. netifd then never finishes loading the
wireless handlers, so no network is configured.

This happens on the Edgecore EAP115/EAP115a with the Morse Micro
HaLow handler installed: netifd stays at 100% CPU on its dump and
no bridge is created.

Leave the loop when the read returns null.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 package/network/config/netifd/files/lib/netifd/utils.uc | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/network/config/netifd/files/lib/netifd/utils.uc b/package/network/config/netifd/files/lib/netifd/utils.uc
index 84db69d2fa..8abf085a8d 100644
--- a/package/network/config/netifd/files/lib/netifd/utils.uc
+++ b/package/network/config/netifd/files/lib/netifd/utils.uc
@@ -55,7 +55,11 @@ export function handler_load(path, cb)
 		chdir(prev_dir);
 		f.seek();
 		while (!f.error()) {
-			let data = trim(f.read("line"));
+			let line = f.read("line");
+			if (line == null)
+				break;
+
+			let data = trim(line);
 			try {
 				data = json(data);
 			} catch (e) {
